in ukraine overnight russia fired more  missiles at the port city of odessa far  beyond the front lines you are looking  now at a shopping mall that was hit  multiple times officials say at least  one person was killed there and several  others were wounded deborah pat is in  ukraine where the reality of the war is  far from what the kremlin is telling the  russian people  russia's distorted reality a jubilant  end to victory day lights up the night  skies above moscow but in ukraine russia  really has nothing to celebrate vladimir  putin's war is failing says acting u.s  ambassador christina kavin it would be  hard to find something that he could  claim victory for frankly  i haven't seen any clear victories at  all in this war so far for president  putin  but he has caused untold misery across  the east and south of the country  in the port city of odessa the jagged  remains of a shopping mall ripped apart  and in the eastern village of seversk  ash's still smolder  it's hard to imagine anything could  survive this nightmare  this elderly woman has endured heavy  shelling she lies flat on her bed to  escape the bombing  my son is dead she weeps i have no one  to protect me  russia is locked in a modern day david  and goliath battle and for all its heavy  artillery it has suffered heavy losses  up north ukrainian forces are pushing  russian troops back from harkeev just  like they did in kiev back in april and  now people are slowly coming back to the  capital  i just came into my house for the first  time today it was a little emotional it  was really special to be back i'm so so  happy to be here  to see all of my old friends  she's not alone amidst all the pain  occasional moments of joy like this  mother who was reunited with her son  after 74 days separated by war  for cbs mornings deborah patter kiev  ukraine
 

